<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Everything else in perch's Info.plist is generated (GENERATE_INFOPLIST_FILE
  is still YES; Xcode merges its keys into this file). This partial exists for
  one key that has no INFOPLIST_KEY_ build setting: NSServices.

  Perch declares two doors into the Finder context menu. MEASURED on macOS 26
  (field-test 2026-08-23), they land in the SAME place: both this NSServices
  entry and the PerchFinderAction extension appear under "Services", and the
  menu shows "Add to Perch Shelf (Perch.app)" twice — macOS only appends the
  app name when it has two providers with one title to tell apart.

  Neither of the older claims survived the measurement. This entry is NOT at
  the menu's top level beside "New Terminal Tab Here", and the extension does
  NOT appear under "Quick Actions" (it is listed and enabled in Quick Actions ▸
  Customize… and in Login Items & Extensions, and still does not render there).
  Verified with exactly one registered copy: `pluginkit -mAvvv -p
  com.apple.services` reports a single plug-in, so the duplicate is these two
  doors and not two builds fighting.

  So keeping both costs a visible duplicate and buys nothing that was claimed
  for it. See the 2026-08-22 field-test file, #4/#5.

  NSRequiredContext is deliberately empty — every restricting key you add is
  another reason for macOS to hide the item, and the send types below are
  already the filter.

  Those send types are wider than Finder on purpose. Keeping the text and URL
  types means selected text or a link in Mail, Safari or an editor offers the
  same command from that app's Services menu, and it lands on the shelf as the
  same staged text a drag would make. Narrowing this to file URLs would buy a
  tidier menu at the cost of the one place a Service beats a drag: sending a
  selection from an app you cannot drag out of.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSServices</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>NSMenuItem</key>
			<dict>
				<key>default</key>
				<string>Add to Perch Shelf</string>
			</dict>
			<key>NSMessage</key>
			<string>addToShelf</string>
			<key>NSPortName</key>
			<string>Perch</string>
			<key>NSRequiredContext</key>
			<dict/>
			<key>NSSendTypes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSFilenamesPboardType</string>
				<string>public.file-url</string>
				<string>public.url</string>
				<string>public.plain-text</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
